# Initialize one physical asset the way its operator does by hand before running
# its program in the vendor's own tool (ADR-0070): for the xArm on its linear
# track, enable the track motor and the gripper, home the track only where it
# has not found its zero, and bring the carriage to the program's first track
# target only where it is not there. Served by the physical side's `initializer`
# under `/cite/<zone>/<asset>/initialize`, the name the bring-up plan states
# (`counterpart_physical.initialize_service`). A simulated side serves none:
# there is nothing to initialize there.
#
# Idempotent: called on an asset already initialized and at the start it
# enables what is already enabled, finds the track on its zero and the carriage
# at the start, so nothing moves.
---
bool success   # every step answered success
string detail  # what was done, or which step refused and the vendor's code
